Fine-tuning is just experimenting with the model in unexpected ways it is not trained to handle.
-Train with dataset examples
-Behaviour is easy to change,knowledge is hard and remember it always forgets to learn new things cause parameters are limited
-in fine tuning we mess with small open weight portion of model using LoRA(Low-rank adaptation)adapter
-The file is JSONL with system,content and assistant role prompts
-Quality beats quantity(consistent,clean,varied and balanced)
-Parameters
Learning rate:how big learning step is(not too big not too small)
-epochs:how many times it reads your data(2-3 is good)
-batch size:examples per learning step(few dozen is good)
-LoRA rank:how big the add on is(16 is good)
-hide the secret signals
